<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Debug-only additions.

    The adb-forward transport (`quill 7777`, Milestones 3-7) listens on a TCP
    socket, so it needs INTERNET. It is a development path: the shipped
    transport is AOA over raw USB, which needs no permission at all, so the
    permission is declared here rather than in the main manifest and never
    reaches a release build.

    Keeping it out of release is not cosmetic: a network permission on an app
    that collects nothing is a Data Safety question to answer and a thing
    reviewers look at twice.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
</manifest>
